1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
John's Twitch Handler brings your stream controls, checks, and highlights into one local Windows dashboard.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:14,000
Before going live, check OBS, Twitch, your microphone, and internet. Add reminders for the things you always want to check.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,000
During the stream, keep scene controls, audio, chat, and replay tools within reach, with Simple and Advanced views to suit your workflow.

4
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:29,000
When something worth saving happens, add a highlight note, save the OBS replay, or create a Twitch clip for later.

5
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,500
Stream health brings performance signals together, helping you spot pressure and understand what may be affecting the broadcast.

6
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:43,750
Choose Broadcast, Vibe, or Tactical styling. Move panels where you want them, and switch between RPG and FPS game profiles.

7
00:00:43,750 --> 00:00:52,250
Afterward, review your session timeline, highlights, and performance events. Export your markers, or hand clips off to StreamLadder for editing.

8
00:00:52,250 --> 00:01:00,000
Your reports and preferences stay on your computer. John's Twitch Handler. Ready for your next stream.
